{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--oblique-incorporation-requires-applicative","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--overview"],"statement":{"en":"In Ainu, oblique nominals cannot be directly incorporated into a verb without first being promoted to a direct object via an applicative prefix.","ja":"アイヌ語において斜格名詞は動詞に直接抱合されることはできず、適用接頭辞によって直接目的語へ昇格された後にのみ抱合されうる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0005-19","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0040-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0041-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0042-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--applicative-internal-to-incorporated-noun","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--overview"],"statement":{"en":"In the incorporation of an oblique nominal via applicative formation, the applicative prefix occurs internally and the incorporated noun is added externally.","ja":"適用詞形成を経た斜格名詞の抱合において、適用接頭辞が内側に、抱合名詞が外側に付加される。"},"type":"ordering","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0042-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--irregular-prefixation-before-incorporated-noun","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--overview"],"statement":{"en":"A small set of irregular forms reported in Chiri (1936) exhibit an order where the applicative prefix precedes the incorporated noun rather than following it.","ja":"知里 (1936) に報告された少数の不規則な形式では、適用接頭辞が抱合名詞の後ではなく前に位置する語順を示す。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["o-ni-pici","o-sik-poso","o-cip-ika"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0044-02","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--applicative-internal-to-incorporated-noun","differs_in":"scope","note":"Irregular lexical forms exhibit the reverse order Appl-N-V instead of N-Appl-V."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--in-poetic-expressions-expletives-can-be-incorporated-into","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate"],"statement":{"en":"In poetic expressions, expletives can be incorporated into verbs, as seen in i=emaknakurraypa kane 'it drove me back', where the element -kur is an incorporated expletive.","ja":"韻文的な表現においては虚辞の抱合がよく見られ、例えば i=emaknakurraypa kane「によって私はたじたじとなった」では -kur が虚辞として抱合されている。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"actual","conditions":["poetic verse"]},"forms":["-kur","i=emaknakurraypa kane"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0480-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--ainu-verbs-cannot-incorporate-other-parts-of-speech","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--correspondences"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu verbs cannot incorporate other parts of speech such as particles or adnominals; functions corresponding to postpositional adverbs like ani and tura, case particles like (or)ta and (or)un, or conjunctional particles like kusu are expressed by applicative affixes.","ja":"アイヌ語では助詞や連体詞などそれ以外の品詞を抱合することはできず、後置副詞 ani や tura、格助詞 (or)ta や (or)un、接続助詞 kusu に相当する意味・文法関係は対応する充当接辞によって表される。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"necessary","conditions":[]},"forms":["ani","tura","ta","un","kusu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0480-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--noun-incorporation-in-ainu-is-simply-one-means","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--debate"],"statement":{"en":"Noun incorporation in Ainu is simply one means of filling an argument slot, eliminating the need to derive it by syntactic head movement from an independent external noun phrase.","ja":"アイヌ語における名詞抱合は「項スロット」の充足方法の1つに過ぎず、自立語を用いた統語的表現からの主要部移動によって派生させる必要はない。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2023b@pdftotext-pieces/l0007-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--the-phrase-ka-opas-literally-run-to-one","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--debate"],"statement":{"en":"The phrase ka opas (literally 'run to one's surface') is an idiomatic quasi-incorporation expression meaning 'save'.","ja":"句 ka opas（逐語訳「〜の表面に走る」）は、「救う」を意味する慣用的な準抱合表現である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ka opas"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:satoni2022@handbook-epub/l0108-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--the-phrase-ka-oyki-literally-do-something-to","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--debate"],"statement":{"en":"The phrase ka oyki (literally 'do something to one's surface') is an idiomatic quasi-incorporation expression meaning 'take care of'.","ja":"句 ka oyki（逐語訳「〜の表面に何かをする」）は、「世話をする」を意味する慣用的な準抱合表現である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ka oyki"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:satoni2022@handbook-epub/l0108-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--the-phrase-kes-anpa-literally-catch-one-s","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--debate"],"statement":{"en":"The phrase kes anpa (literally 'catch one's end') is an idiomatic quasi-incorporation expression meaning 'chase'.","ja":"句 kes anpa（逐語訳「〜の端を捕らえる」）は、「追跡する」を意味する慣用的な準抱合表現である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kes anpa"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:satoni2022@handbook-epub/l0108-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--the-phrase-tom-oytak-literally-talk-to-one","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--debate"],"statement":{"en":"The phrase tom oytak (literally 'talk to one's center') is an idiomatic quasi-incorporation expression meaning 'persuade'.","ja":"句 tom oytak（逐語訳「〜の中心に話す」）は、「説得する」を意味する慣用的な準抱合表現である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["tom oytak"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:satoni2022@handbook-epub/l0108-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--the-phrase-aske-uk-literally-take-one-s","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--debate"],"statement":{"en":"The phrase aske uk (literally 'take one's hand') is an idiomatic quasi-incorporation expression meaning 'invite'.","ja":"句 aske uk（逐語訳「〜の手を取る」）は、「招く」を意味する慣用的な準抱合表現である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["aske uk"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:satoni2022@handbook-epub/l0108-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--the-phrase-par-oyki-literally-do-something-to","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--debate"],"statement":{"en":"The phrase par oyki (literally 'do something to one's mouth') is an idiomatic quasi-incorporation expression meaning 'feed' or 'support'.","ja":"句 par oyki（逐語訳「〜の口に何かをする」）は、「養う、支援する」を意味する慣用的な準抱合表現である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["par oyki"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:satoni2022@handbook-epub/l0108-10","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--in-compound-verb-structures-of-the-type-objective","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--overview"],"statement":{"en":"In compound verb structures of the type 'objective prefix + noun + transitive verb', the incorporated noun is normally a locative noun or a body part.","ja":"「目的格的接頭辞＋名詞＋他動詞」の型の語形成に現れる名詞は、位置名詞か身体部位であるのが普通である。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0307-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--the-verb-yayramtomoytak-to-calm-one-s-feelings","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The verb yayramtomoytak 'to calm one's feelings/anger' is morphologically analyzed as yay- 'self (acc.)' + ram 'heart/mind' + tom 'middle' + o- 'at/towards' + itak 'speak'.","ja":"動詞 yayramtomoytak「自分の気持ち（怒り）を静める」は、yay-「自分を」＋ ram「心」＋ tom「真ん中」＋ o-「に」＋ itak「話す」と分析される。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["yayramtomoytak","yay-","ram","tom","o-","itak"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0327-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--an-independent-noun-stem-such-as-upsor-bosom","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--overview"],"statement":{"en":"An independent noun stem such as upsor 'bosom' can be incorporated into the locative slot of omare 'put into' in place of the nominal prefix u-, leaving the subject and theme slots to be filled by transitive inflection (e.g. kane k-upsor-omare 'I put money into my bosom').","ja":"omare「入れる」の場所のスロットには、名詞的接頭辞 u- の代わりに upsor「ふところ」のような自立語基を抱合することができ、主語と主題のスロットは他動詞活用によって充足される（例: kane k-upsor-omare）。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["upsor","omare"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2023b@pdftotext-pieces/l0008-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--when-applicative-formation-and-noun-incorporation-apply-to","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--overview"],"statement":{"en":"When applicative formation and noun incorporation apply to the same semantically oblique nominal, the derivation proceeds via applicative formation advancing the oblique to object before noun incorporation applies.","ja":"適用構文形成と名詞抱合が同一の意味的斜格名詞に適用される場合、適用構文形成によって斜格が目的語になった後に名詞抱合が適用されるという順序で派生する。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["involving the same nominal"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0043-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--oblique-nominal-adjuncts-cannot-be-incorporated-directly-into","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topics":["topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate","topic:valency/noun-incorporation-oblique-polysynthesis-debate--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Oblique nominal adjuncts cannot be incorporated directly into the verb.","ja":"斜格名詞付加詞は動詞に直接抱合されることはできない。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"none","modality":"necessary","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0044-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
